 "_doc": [
  "FLOATSPELL \u2014 the one spelling of a full-precision f64 both ports must",
  "write. RULED 2026-08-05 (fleet/RULING-four-decimal-floor): the transform",
  "matrix goes to full precision, and 'full precision' has no single",
  "spelling \u2014 Rust's Display writes 1e-7 as 0.0000001 while Swift writes",
  "1e-07, and Swift writes integral values with a trailing '.0' that Rust",
  "omits. The 4dp floor was accidentally shielding both ports because",
  "{:.4} is fixed-notation in both; removing it would have made the two",
  "ports write DIFFERENT FILES for the same document.",
  "",
  "THE RULE: the shortest decimal that round-trips, in FIXED notation,",
  "never exponent, no trailing '.0'.",
  "",
  "Expected values are computed in Python from that DEFINITION, not read",
  "out of either port, so this corpus can catch either one."
 ],
